  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Testosterone is an androgen, the primary male sex hormone, used to treat conditions such as hypogonadism and Klinefelter's syndrome. It is an approved medicine, though some products have been withdrawn in the European Union, and it also has investigational uses.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1318776\">Wikidata Q1318776</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>testosterone</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>G03BA03</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00624\">DB00624</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/6013\">6013</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:17347\">17347</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1318776\">Q1318776</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C19H28O2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>288.431 g/mol (PubChem CID 6013)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>3.3 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
